    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answer: $84920$.",
      "worked": "A number is divisible by 11 when the difference between its alternating digit sums is a multiple of 11.\n\nFor $84920$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(8+9+0)-(4+2)&=17-6\\\\(8+9+0)-(4+2)&=11\\end{align*}$$\nSo $84920$ is divisible by 11.\n\nAll eight possibilities are $14520$, $24420$, $34320$, $44220$, $54120$, $64020$, $84920$ and $94820$.",
